; A spec whose only cross-scope reference into `c` runs THROUGH a named collection defined in `a`.
;
; The projection resolves a named collection through at its use sites — `names` is never a WIT type
; — so the emitted package links `b -> c` (the ELEMENT's scope) and never `b -> a`, and the `a` rule
; `names` links nothing at all. A cycle walk that recorded the collection ident instead would see
; `b -> a` and `a -> c` beside the real `c -> a`, closing a cycle in a spec whose WIT resolves
; perfectly — a refusal naming scopes the emitted package never links, which a user cannot act on.
; This fixture must GENERATE; `a_real_cycle_through_a_named_collection_is_still_rejected` covers the
; other direction, so the agreement is pinned from both sides.

root = { r: rec }
